  "body": "## What\n\nAdds the parent-level Atlas ingestion-operations design record for #6019: `doc/2026-11-09T05-12-00Z_design_atlas_ingestion_operations/`.\n\nDesign only — no product code, no schedule created.\n\n## Contents (per #6019 acceptance)\n\n- §1 Sibling reconciliation, revalidated fresh 2026-11-09: settled — #6026, #6043, #6058 (closed since the packet was written), #6060, #6061; open inputs — #6028, #6045, #6057, #6059 — with what this record takes from each.\n- §2 Per-source table for boot/reboot records, session logs, chats, statistics, reports (+ code-repo): trigger model, usefulness/inclusion test, rejection logging with a closed reason-code set, and the human approval gates that make it *semi*-automated. Secret-tier items are held, never hosted-embedded, until #6059 lands.\n- §3 Pipeline seams: delta-only discovery (#6028) → filter → content-addressed staging landing (#3125, #5669) → gate promotion (#6057); sweeps never delete and never promote.\n- §4 Disk/I/O guardrails: measurement points on source and target hosts, initial-slot thresholds, throttle / pause / abort behaviour, alert names.\n- §5 Plan-headroom accounting against the Turso scaler envelope ($24.92/mo): per-run/per-source report fields (embedding spend referenced from the #6058 ledger, never recomputed), the #6061 70%-projection rule, 80% alert, 95% ceiling stop — no silent spend, plan changes are human decisions.\n- §6 Recurring sweep runbook: cadence shape, per-(class, host) locking, content-addressed idempotence, bounded backfill with approval bounds, partial-failure/dead-letter handling, operator actions.\n- §7 Follow-up audit: exactly one parent-level gap has no ticket (the sweep runner + guardrail monitor + reporting); filed as a separate implementation issue linked from #6019. No duplicate child issues.\n\n## Verification\n\nDesign-only task: current-main document review + fresh GitHub state checks for all nine siblings (states and merged records verified 2026-11-09). Follows the dated-record convention in `doc/README.md` (one folder per design record). Like the other 2026-11-08/09 atlas records, no architecture-index line is added.\n\nRefs #6019. Queue task 14270 (lane code-l).\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796793182&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7968&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7968&signature=bf895ce94723563ac8c5f8f9d147626faf67b94741967cf492117a22d8499e4e\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7968?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
